  - .assets/img-102-01-07.png

steps:
  - cmds: []
    text: |
      {[ht,$start]Welcome}

      TODO: Position this group as the first larger EMS program after Orientation and Basic Examples.

      TODO: Explain that CoreMark starts as a real embedded C benchmark, and this group shows how that benchmark is re-rendered into EMS modules while preserving validation behavior.

      TODO: Mention that the tour run is intentionally short and observable, not yet a formal published CoreMark score.

  - cmds:
      - open 1
      - mark 1 A 19
      - mark 1 B 51
      - mark 1 C 88
    focus: [1,88]
    text: |
      {[ht,$look]Legacy Sources}

      TODO: Give the reader a quick look at the original CoreMark C harness without doing a line-by-line reading.

      {[bm,A]} TODO: Identify this as the original {[cd]core_main.c} framework.

      {[bm,B]} TODO: Point out the benchmark iteration function.

      {[bm,C]} TODO: Point out the traditional C {[cd]main()} harness and its setup/run/report responsibilities.

      TODO: Link or mention the official CoreMark source set and explain that later tours can compare individual EMS workload modules against the corresponding C files.

  - cmds:
      - close 1
      - view 2
    text: |
      {[ht,$details]Module Map}

      TODO: Use this diagram as the roadmap for the CoreMark in EMS group.

      TODO: Explain the active path first: {[cd]ActiveRunnerP} calls the shared {[cd]CoreBench} engine.

