  - cmds:
      - mark 3 A 29
    focus: [3,29]
    acts: ['$build']
    text: |
      {[ht,$build]ActiveRunner Output}

      TODO: Interpret the output that appears after building and running the program.

      {[bm,A]} TODO: Connect this printf block to the five terminal lines:

      {[cd]usecs = ...}
      {[cd]list crc = ...}
      {[cd]matrix crc = ...}
      {[cd]state crc = ...}
      {[cd]final crc = ...}

      TODO: Explain that {[cd]usecs} is a real elapsed-time measurement for this short configured run, while the CRCs are the correctness checks that keep the EMS rendering honest.

      TODO: Optionally mention the build size reported by the tools: larger than Basic Examples, still tiny for a real benchmark-style program.

  - cmds: []
    text: |
      {[ht,$extra]Extra Credit}

